---
layout: base.njk
title: "Download DHUN — rolling test build for Android and Windows"
ogTitle: "Download DHUN"
description: "Download the rolling DHUN test build: a universal APK for Android 7.0+, ABI splits, and a Windows installer that needs a system VLC install. Each file ships with a SHA-256 sidecar to verify before installing."
cssModules: ["tokens", "base", "components", "download"]
---
<div class="wrap">
  <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="dl-title">
    <span class="kicker">ROLLING TEST BUILD</span>
    <h1 id="dl-title">{{ site.downloads.title }}</h1>
    <p class="hero-lead">{{ site.downloads.intro }}</p>
    <!-- REQUIRED CAVEAT: the artifact's real status, stated before the links. -->
    <div class="notice" data-caveat="rolling-unverified">
      <p><strong>Rolling UNVERIFIED development build.</strong> These files are
      replaced on every push to <code>main</code> and are signed with the
      public test key committed to the repository
      (<code>app-android/keystores/dhun-test.p12</code>). Anyone with the
      repository can mint a same-key APK, so install only from the links on
      this page or the GitHub release page.</p>
      <!-- README.md test-builds policy; app-android/keystores/dhun-test.p12; test-release.yml -->
    </div>
    <p class="traceable">The three APKs are ABI splits of one build, not three different versions — they are not byte-identical, which is why each has its own checksum sidecar. DHUN bundles no native code.</p>
    <!--PR #131 (minSdk 24 + three test APKs); README.md -->
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="files-title">
    <h2 id="files-title">Files</h2>
    <!-- test-release.yml: these four asset names are what the rolling `test` release always carries; only their bytes change. -->
    <p class="lede">
      No digest or file size is printed here on purpose: those bytes change on
      every merge to <code>main</code>, and a stale hash on a marketing page is
      worse than no hash at all. Download the <code>.sha256</code> sidecar next
      to each file and compare before installing.
    </p>
    <ul class="asset-list">
      {%- for asset in site.downloads.assets %}
      <li>
        <div class="asset{% if asset.recommended %} asset--recommended{% endif %}">
          <div class="asset-head">
            <span class="asset-name">{{ asset.name }}</span>
            {%- if asset.recommended %}
            <span class="asset-tag asset-tag--primary">RECOMMENDED</span>
            {%- endif %}
            {%- if asset.kind == "android" %}
            <span class="asset-tag">ANDROID 7.0+</span>
            {%- else %}
            <span class="asset-tag">WINDOWS</span>
            {%- endif %}
          </div>
          <p><strong>{{ asset.label }}.</strong> {{ asset.detail }}</p>
          <div class="asset-links">
            <a class="btn btn--primary" href="{{ asset.url }}" rel="noopener">Download {{ asset.name }}<span class="ext" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "download" %}</span></a>
            <a class="sha" href="{{ asset.sha256Url }}" rel="noopener">Get the .sha256 sidecar</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
    <p class="traceable">Assets on the GitHub release page:
      <a href="{{ site.testReleasePage }}" rel="noopener">releases/tag/test</a> — the same files, listed by GitHub.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="install-title">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2 id="install-title">Install</h2>
      <p class="lede">Three steps, in this order. The checksum step is the one people skip and regret.</p>
    </div>
    <ol class="steps">
      {%- for step in site.downloads.steps %}
      <li>
        <h3>{{ step.title }}</h3>
        <p>{{ step.body }}</p>
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ol>
    <!--AndroidManifest.xml permissions; MASTER_PROMPT §4 (no telemetry) -->
    <div class="notice" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
      <p><strong>What it asks for.</strong> {{ site.install.permissions }}</p>
      <p><strong>What it never sends.</strong> {{ site.install.privacy }}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="missing-title">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2 id="missing-title">What is not on this page</h2>
    <!-- MASTER_PROMPT §1 and §7 ("Explicitly NOT in S1–S6"): no store channel, no iOS, no web client, no stable release. -->
      <p class="lede">A download page that lists what does not exist is more useful than one that quietly omits it.</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="missing">
      {%- for item in site.downloads.notAvailable %}
      <li>{{ item }}</li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="source-title">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2 id="source-title">{{ site.downloads.buildIt.title }}</h2>
      <p class="lede">{{ site.downloads.buildIt.body }}</p>
      <!--{{ site.downloads.buildIt.source }}-->
    </div>
    <pre><code>{%- for command in site.downloads.buildIt.commands %}
{{ command }}
{%- endfor %}</code></pre>
    <p class="traceable">{{ site.downloads.technicalNote }}</p>
  </section>

  <!-- REQUIRED CAVEAT: the hardware gates are open. -->
  <section class="risk" aria-labelledby="gates-title" data-caveat="hardware-gates-open">
    <h2 id="gates-title">What "test build" means for you</h2>
    <p>Android and Windows acceptance on real hardware (S3 in the project's
    plan) is <strong>not finished</strong>. The open items — a compact docked
    mini-player pass on Android and Windows, and an install on an Android
    7.0–7.1 device — are tracked in the repository rather than softened here.</p>
    <p>There is also no stable release to fall back to: the honest state is one
    rolling pre-release plus the source.</p>
    <!--MASTER_PROMPT §7 Stage S3; .ai/ROADMAP.md current gates; .ai/KNOWN_LIMITATIONS.md -->
    <p><a href="{{ site.changelog }}" rel="noopener">CHANGELOG.md</a> ·
       <a href="{{ site.repo }}/blob/main/.ai/KNOWN_LIMITATIONS.md" rel="noopener">Known limitations</a> ·
       <a href="{{ site.risk.link.href }}" rel="noopener">ADR-001: the maintenance contract</a></p>
  </section>
</div>
